WEBVTT

00:00.050 --> 00:03.000
As I told you, in this video I'll show you

00:03.050 --> 00:06.000
how we can enter our meals

00:06.050 --> 00:09.000
and manage them in general.

00:09.050 --> 00:12.000
We tap the left area here,

00:12.050 --> 00:15.000
where, as you can see, I've
already entered two meals

00:15.050 --> 00:18.000
of my own today.

00:18.050 --> 00:23.050
Tapping on one, I see the
details of each meal.

00:33.050 --> 00:35.050
So, how does it work?

00:36.050 --> 00:42.456
Tapping here, then, if I
want to enter a meal, a set

00:42.456 --> 00:48.000
of foods I ate at some
other time of the day,

00:48.050 --> 00:53.050
I tap the plus and choose "Add
meal details", or "Add kcal

00:53.050 --> 00:58.050
only" if I want to be quick
and not say which foods I ate.

00:59.050 --> 01:02.050
I'll choose the first one
here: "Add meal details".

01:03.050 --> 01:09.050
Up here I set the time
and date I ate my meal.

01:11.580 --> 01:15.530
By default it suggests the
date and time of entry.

01:15.580 --> 01:21.694
And tapping the plus
here, I can pick what I

01:21.694 --> 01:27.530
want from the food categories the app has.

01:27.580 --> 01:30.693
Rather than browsing
category by category, we

01:30.693 --> 01:33.530
can go here, where it says "Choose food",

01:33.580 --> 01:38.382
and type, this time
let's type the word for,

01:38.382 --> 01:42.530
uh, yogurt; you see I've typed "γιαο",

01:42.580 --> 01:45.330
I haven't typed the "ύ" yet.

01:45.380 --> 01:48.390
You see, the yogurt dessert appears,

01:48.440 --> 01:51.400
as well as, under "Cheese, Milk

01:51.820 --> 01:54.740
and Dairy", the three yogurts the app has.

01:55.800 --> 01:58.260
But (I mention it because we had

01:58.340 --> 02:00.100
some questions today)

02:00.380 --> 02:02.500
if I type the "ύ" with the accent,

02:03.220 --> 02:05.340
you see, it shows only

02:06.220 --> 02:08.050
the first one, the yogurt dessert,

02:08.100 --> 02:10.710
because that entry has

02:10.760 --> 02:13.000
the accented "ύ" in its name.

02:14.200 --> 02:18.230
If I delete it,

02:18.280 --> 02:20.490
the other two show up again.

02:20.540 --> 02:22.990
The other three, rather.

02:23.040 --> 02:24.240
You see here

02:36.140 --> 02:37.520
what the difference is.

02:38.200 --> 02:41.570
When I type it with the accent,
it finds only the yogurt dessert.

02:41.620 --> 02:44.720
When I type the "υ" without the accent,

02:45.140 --> 02:48.420
it finds the yogurts: it depends
on how the word is written.

02:48.880 --> 02:51.840
Here, with the X, we clear

02:53.640 --> 02:54.990
what we had typed.

02:55.040 --> 03:06.086
If I want the app to search one of the
international databases (first I clear

03:06.086 --> 03:15.840
the field, once and for all), I can
type here, for example, the word

03:15.890 --> 03:23.840
"cheese", for example, and tap the globe,

03:23.890 --> 03:29.890
and the app searches the
international databases:

03:30.890 --> 03:34.890
the US one, the first it found, and a
French one I'll show you in a moment,

03:36.890 --> 03:38.090
this one here,

03:38.890 --> 03:44.840
where you see it found 84,261
entries in the French one

03:44.890 --> 03:46.840
containing the word "cheese",

03:46.890 --> 03:51.840
and about 60,000 entries in the US one.

03:51.890 --> 03:57.840
These are the first hundred of the
French one; in a moment you'll see

03:57.890 --> 04:02.840
the photos of the different
foods appear here on the right.

04:02.890 --> 04:07.840
I can also look at each one in
detail: this is such-and-such food.

04:07.890 --> 04:12.840
We don't usually use these.

04:12.890 --> 04:17.840
What we do use (and let me show
you a trick while we're at it):

04:17.890 --> 04:24.840
tapping the X twice reloads
our database from scratch.

04:24.890 --> 04:28.840
I mean, if we've entered something
and don't see it in the food list,

04:28.890 --> 04:34.840
say we go here, to Foods,
enter it, and come back,

04:34.890 --> 04:37.840
it won't show up here at once,
but if we tap it once or twice,

04:37.890 --> 04:40.840
the database is reloaded and it shows up.

04:40.890 --> 04:42.840
Now let's enter, say, eggs.

04:42.890 --> 04:45.640
I ate an egg: we choose "Egg, large".

04:45.690 --> 04:47.640
Here we tap one, two eggs, three eggs.

04:47.690 --> 04:52.460
And it seems that here,

04:52.510 --> 04:55.460
with the changes I made recently,

04:55.510 --> 04:57.460
the 3 doesn't show very well.

04:57.510 --> 04:59.510
In this...

05:01.510 --> 05:06.980
Let's switch to the Natura theme.

05:07.030 --> 05:10.260
Eggs, then: one, two, three.

05:10.310 --> 05:12.260
There.

05:12.310 --> 05:13.260
We tap OK.

05:13.310 --> 05:18.710
Hmm, let me see.

05:18.760 --> 05:25.450
Eggs, eggs,

05:25.500 --> 05:27.450
we tap...

05:27.500 --> 05:33.770
Eggs, three eggs and OK.

05:33.820 --> 05:36.414
It tells me the three eggs have this much

05:36.414 --> 05:39.450
protein, this much fat,
this many calories, etc.

05:39.500 --> 05:44.250
I can add more foods and
build up my meal this way.

05:44.300 --> 05:46.490
Bread, say, etc.

05:46.540 --> 05:50.890
Bread: a slice, or half a slice, etc.

05:50.940 --> 05:59.450
OK, I select the entries and delete them,

05:59.500 --> 06:02.450
because I don't want to keep them.

06:02.500 --> 06:06.290
The other feature I want to
show you, added recently,

06:06.340 --> 06:13.310
is a very handy feature
added lately to the app:

06:13.360 --> 06:16.860
the app can, from a photo

06:17.340 --> 06:20.690
of the plate you're eating, or of
the plates you're about to eat,

06:20.740 --> 06:24.230
find the ingredients on the plate:

06:24.280 --> 06:27.700
whether it has meat and how much,
potatoes and how much, and so on,

06:27.780 --> 06:30.680
pasta, etc. I'll show you now, here.

06:31.140 --> 06:32.340
We tap here:

06:32.440 --> 06:35.130
"Meal from photo". I
tap the second option,

06:35.180 --> 06:39.200
because I've taken a few photos
of food: "Choose from gallery".

06:39.540 --> 06:42.550
And I tap this one here
which, as you can see,

06:42.600 --> 06:45.480
is chicken with potatoes
and a little feta cheese.

06:45.620 --> 06:48.470
I've also put my finger
in the picture, so as

06:48.520 --> 06:54.230
to let the artificial
intelligence agent that is used

06:54.280 --> 06:58.390
estimate the size of the plate and how

06:58.440 --> 07:00.630
far or near the photo was taken,

07:00.680 --> 07:06.790
since it can't perceive depth.

07:06.840 --> 07:11.250
That said, it isn't necessary:

07:11.300 --> 07:14.210
three other photos have no
hand; it estimates them well.

07:14.260 --> 07:18.450
So I choose this plate.

07:18.500 --> 07:22.313
The app now recognises
the foods, and in 2 to 3

07:22.313 --> 07:26.450
seconds it will tell me
what it found on the plate.

07:26.500 --> 07:33.450
And what did it find? Here: roast
chicken with skin, 250 grams, etc.,

07:33.500 --> 07:37.344
roast potatoes, feta,
grilled aubergine, and

07:37.344 --> 07:41.450
further down some notes
that are worth reading.

07:41.500 --> 07:46.754
If I want to add the meal,
because it estimated

07:46.754 --> 07:51.450
its ingredients well, I tap "Add to meal".

07:51.500 --> 07:56.374
If it added something by
mistake, I can tap it here and

07:56.374 --> 08:00.450
choose "Delete"; usually
that won't be needed.

08:00.500 --> 08:05.026
There. I go back, where
it tells me the meal

08:05.026 --> 08:09.450
list isn't empty, to
save it or discard it,

08:09.500 --> 08:12.785
and I tap "Discard" because,
as I told you, I use the

08:12.785 --> 08:15.450
app myself and don't
want to spoil my data.

08:15.500 --> 08:21.450
So let's go here to the details and
enter another food from a photo.

08:21.500 --> 08:24.752
In this photo, say, I've
put a Sokofreta wafer,

08:24.752 --> 08:27.450
a petit four and a loukoumi on a plate.

08:27.500 --> 08:32.450
If you choose it, you'll see it
recognised them all accurately:

08:32.500 --> 08:40.560
Sokofreta, a chocolate-dipped
biscuit and a coconut sweet.

08:40.610 --> 08:44.560
There. Cancel: I don't add it.

08:44.610 --> 08:47.838
Another photo is here, where
I've put a piece, just

08:47.838 --> 08:50.560
two small pieces of
chocolate on the plate.

08:50.610 --> 08:52.560
Two small pieces of chocolate.

08:52.610 --> 08:55.205
And it tells me: on the plate
there are two squares of

08:55.205 --> 08:57.560
chocolate with a logo that
can't be read clearly.

08:57.610 --> 09:00.560
The weight is an estimate.

09:00.610 --> 09:04.560
It says they weigh 12 grams
and have 70 calories.

09:04.610 --> 09:09.560
I could add them, or I
select them and delete them.

09:09.610 --> 09:18.510
And one last food, the very last: what
did I put here? I don't remember,

09:18.560 --> 09:22.510
I didn't look closely.
It was Greek yogurt,

09:22.560 --> 09:29.510
which it estimated at 240 grams,
6.7% fat, very precisely.

09:29.560 --> 09:35.030
Let's delete it,

09:35.080 --> 09:40.520
and look at the other food,
which here is a bunch of grapes,

09:41.560 --> 09:44.180
which it analyses

09:44.440 --> 09:47.220
and sees that they're red grapes,

09:47.800 --> 09:49.660
which I add to the meal.

09:50.340 --> 09:53.040
So that's it: this is how
I put together my meals.

09:54.620 --> 10:00.020
In the next and last video, I'll
show you how we enter activities.

10:00.280 --> 10:01.480
Goodbye.
